@prefix : <http://w3id.org/circularfactory/FlexConveyor#> .
@prefix cfc: <http://w3id.org/circularfactory/Core#> .
@prefix svc: <http://w3id.org/circularfactory/Service#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# The design of this ontology:
#
# - `cfc:` is the published Core (http://w3id.org/circularfactory/Core#), which the middleware
#   loads.
# - Possession is Core's reified `cfc:PossessionState`, written by the middleware's handover, so
#   `:Box` is a `cfc:Workpiece`.
# - The workflow classes are `svc:Workflow` directly. No class-level link runs from
#   `:FlexConveyorModule` or `:WarehouseManagementSystem` to a workflow class: `svc:hasWorkflow`
#   runs from a Service, so such a link would type both classes as services. The middleware links
#   each running service to its workflows when it registers them.
# - The alignment the middleware checks at registration is stated directly: each service class
#   under `svc:Service`, each workflow class under `svc:Workflow`, each capability class under
#   `cfc:Capability`. The check reads one `rdfs:subClassOf` triple and does not follow a chain.
# - `:BoxTransportOperation` is the job of carrying one box, one individual per box, under
#   `cfc:Operation`. `:hasBox`, `:hasOrigin` and `:hasDestination` apply to it. Its status is the
#   middleware's `svc:hasOperationStatus`. The object-graph mapper finds a property of a class only
#   by its `rdfs:domain`, so each of these properties declares one.
# - No module calls a workflow of the WarehouseManagementSystem. The destination module notifies
#   the WarehouseManagementSystem through the middleware once the box is back, and the
#   WarehouseManagementSystem checks the graph.
# - `:BoxTransportCapability` and `:BoxTransportWorkflow`: every module provides the capability to
#   carry a box's transport on, realized by its workflow. A `:BoxTransportOperation` is assigned
#   to one module at a time: Core's `cfc:executedOn` names that module, and the operation
#   implements that module's capability.
# - A box has no lifecycle state of its own. The transport's status and the box's possessor say
#   where the journey is and where the box is, and a change writes each fact once.
# - `:hasHandoverEventStream`: where a module's or the WarehouseManagementSystem's handover event
#   stream is served. Each participant commits it at startup, and a monitor finds the streams
#   through it.
# - `:hasTransport`: the link from a box to its transport, the inverse of `:hasBox`. The
#   transport's opening writes both directions, so a module that holds a box reads its transport
#   through the box, and no party finds a transport from the box's name.
# - A hop between two modules works like the real FlexConveyor: the giving module asks the
#   receiving module's Reserve, commits the handover, conveys the box, a move of its own, and
#   calls the receiving module's Receive, its light barrier, from which the receiving module
#   carries the box on. The comments of `:BoxTransportOperation` and `:BoxTransportWorkflow` say
#   so.
# - A module's convey is its own move, which no party calls, so no module exposes a workflow or a
#   capability for it. The WarehouseManagementSystem spawns a box directly on its origin: it asks
#   the origin's Reserve, creates the box there with its transport in one commit, and notifies the
#   origin. The comment of `:BoxTransportOperation` says so.
# - On the station only the module a transport is assigned to writes it: the module that passed
#   the box on writes nothing when it cannot reach the receiving module's Receive, and the
#   receiving module ends the transport at the bound of its reservation, or at its stop. The
#   comment of `:BoxTransportOperation` says so.
#
# The `fc:` namespace keeps its http scheme, because the paper prints it.

#################################################################
# Ontology
#################################################################

: rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "FlexConveyor System Ontology" ;
    rdfs:comment "Domain ontology for the FlexConveyor material handling system" .

#################################################################
# Classes
#################################################################

:FlexConveyorModule rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cfc:Resource .

:EntryModule rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :FlexConveyorModule .

:ExitModule rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :FlexConveyorModule .

:WarehouseManagementSystem rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cfc:Resource .

:Box rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cfc:Workpiece .

:Connection rdf:type owl:Class .

:BoxTransportOperation rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cfc:Operation ;
    rdfs:comment "The job of carrying one box: from its origin module, where the WarehouseManagementSystem spawns it, to its destination module, and back to the WarehouseManagementSystem. The WarehouseManagementSystem opens it, in the commit that creates the box on the origin, and the handover that brings the box back completes it. It is assigned to one module at a time, the one that carries the box on now: cfc:executedOn names that module, and the operation implements that module's BoxTransportCapability. Both move to the next module in the handover that passes the box. Its status is svc:hasOperationStatus: queued until the origin carries the box on, running while the box travels, done once it is back, failed when the party that cannot go on ends it: a module on the station, or the WarehouseManagementSystem when it cannot notify the origin. On the station only the module it is assigned to writes it: a receiving module whose reservation for the box has passed its bound, or whose stop has begun, with the box its own but no Receive called ends it, and the module that passed the box on writes nothing when it cannot reach the receiving module's Receive." .

#################################################################
# Services
#################################################################

:FlexConveyorModuleService rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf svc:Service ;
    rdfs:comment "The service that wraps one FlexConveyorModule, hosted by its own middleware instance." .

:WarehouseManagementSystemService rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf svc:Service ;
    rdfs:comment "The service that wraps the WarehouseManagementSystem, hosted by its own middleware instance." .

#################################################################
# Workflow Classes
#################################################################

:ReserveWorkflow rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf svc:Workflow .

:ReceiveWorkflow rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf svc:Workflow .

:SpawnBoxWorkflow rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf svc:Workflow .

:SetSpawnRateWorkflow rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf svc:Workflow .

:BoxTransportWorkflow rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf svc:Workflow ;
    rdfs:comment "The workflow of a FlexConveyorModule that carries a box's transport on while the transport is assigned to the module: it starts the transport at the origin, passes the box and the transport to the next module, and gives the box back to the WarehouseManagementSystem at the destination. It realizes the module's BoxTransportCapability. At the origin, the WarehouseManagementSystem's notification of the transport starts it; at every later module, the module's Receive does, the light barrier that the giving module calls once it has committed the handover that passes the box and the transport and has conveyed the box, its own move: the receiving module then reads the box with its transport." .

#################################################################
# Capability Classes
#################################################################

:ReserveCapability rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cfc:Capability .

:ReceiveCapability rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cfc:Capability .

:SpawnBoxCapability rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cfc:Capability .

:SetSpawnRateCapability rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cfc:Capability .

:BoxTransportCapability rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf cfc:Capability ;
    rdfs:comment "The capability of a FlexConveyorModule to carry a box's transport on. Every module provides one, realized by its BoxTransportWorkflow, and a BoxTransportOperation implements the one of the module it is assigned to." .

#################################################################
# Other Domain-Specific Classes
#################################################################

:Direction rdf:type owl:Class .

:North rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :Direction .
:South rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :Direction .
:East  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :Direction .
:West  rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :Direction .

#################################################################
# Object Properties
#################################################################

:hasConnection rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :FlexConveyorModule ;
    rdfs:range :Connection .

:connectsTo rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Connection ;
    rdfs:range :FlexConveyorModule .

:hasOrigin rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :BoxTransportOperation ;
    rdfs:range :FlexConveyorModule .

:hasDestination rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :BoxTransportOperation ;
    rdfs:range :FlexConveyorModule .

:hasBox rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :BoxTransportOperation ;
    rdfs:range :Box .

:hasTransport rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Box ;
    rdfs:range :BoxTransportOperation ;
    owl:inverseOf :hasBox ;
    rdfs:comment "The transport of a box: the BoxTransportOperation that carries it, the inverse of hasBox. The WarehouseManagementSystem's opening of a transport writes both directions, and so does the seed's placing of a box, so a party that holds a box reads the box with its transport in one fetch and finds the transport by no naming rule." .

:hasDirection rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Connection ;
    rdfs:range :Direction .

#################################################################
# Datatype Properties
#################################################################

:onPort rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Connection ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

:hasX rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :FlexConveyorModule ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

:hasY rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :FlexConveyorModule ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

:hasTransitTime rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :FlexConveyorModule ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:label "has transit time" ;
    rdfs:comment "The time in seconds that the module takes to convey a box. 0 means that it conveys at once, with no wait. Each module of a launched topology has exactly one." .

:hasHandoverEventStream rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  owl:unionOf ( :FlexConveyorModule :WarehouseManagementSystem ) ] ;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI ;
    rdfs:comment "Where the participant serves its handover event stream: the URL of an SSE route. The graph holds only where the stream lives, never its events; a reader finds the stream here and reads the events from the participant." .
